    "content": "Jl,. J4 Wei wu wei. This paradoxical expression is  the  key  to Chinese  mysticism.  It  cannot  be  translated literally  and still  render  its meaning. W  ei is  a  verb  corre­ sponding to the English do or act but sometimes meaning other  things,  depending on the expression. Wu is  a  nega­ tive.  Thus,  clumsily, wei  wu  wei is to  do  without  doing, to act without action. Put positively,  it  means to get along as nature does: the  world gets  created,  living things grow and pass away without any sign of effort.",
