    "source_locator": "b9ed361e-8b68-54b8-82d0-f3ec9ad30b89#page=181",
    "content": "Line 1 in the standard text is “Tao invariably takes no action, and yet there is nothing left undone.”This is one of two places in the standard text—the other one beingchapter 48—where the phrasewu-wei erh wu pu-wei, “does nothing and yet there is nothing left undone,” occurs (in some editions of the text the phrase is also found inchapters 3and38). Line 1 is quite different in the Ma-wang-tui texts; in fact lines 1, 2, and 3 here are virtually identical to lines 1, 3, and 4 inchapter 32.",
